# SahajCloud API origin (the widget appends `/api`). Override in .env.local for
# local backend development, e.g. VITE_SAHAJCLOUD_URL="http://localhost:3000".
VITE_SAHAJCLOUD_URL="https://cloud.sydevelopers.com"

# Sentry DSN for automatic error reporting. Intentionally NOT set here, and not a
# secret either — a DSN is write-only and ships in every client bundle. The reason it
# stays out of the repo is noise: committed, every fork, every preview deploy and every
# `pnpm dev` would post into the production project. Set it per-trigger in Workers Builds.
# Unset, the widget logs failures to the console exactly as it did before and never
# fetches the SDK. See docs/environment.md.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=""
#
# VITE_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT tags each event with its deploy. Preview only; defaults to
# `production`. See docs/environment.md.
# VITE_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=""
#
# Source-map upload (#130) is switched on by SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN + SENTRY_ORG +
# SENTRY_PROJECT, which are BUILD-TIME only and so carry no VITE_ prefix — the token is a
# real secret and must never reach the bundle. They are not set here and never should be:
# unset, no maps are emitted at all and the build is byte-identical to one from before
# #130. Set them on every Workers Builds trigger that builds the app; the runbook is in
# docs/environment.md.


# Where a FRAMED embed's "Expand map" sends a visitor (#161). A frame cannot expand —
# `position: fixed` resolves against the frame — so there the button is an anchor to somewhere
# that fits, opened in a new tab.
#
# Public by design. It is a DEFAULT, not a decision: per-region canonical ownership
# (SahajCloud #634) will make the right destination the owner's own site, and this stands in
# until a client record can answer.
#
# NOTE the link carries no route today — an appended ?atlas= is dropped (#252). Why, in
# docs/environment.md.
VITE_WEMEDITATE_MAP_URL="https://wemeditate.com/map"
